Let $V$ be a connected smooth projective manifold and let $i:L\to\Omega_V^p$ be a nonzero line-bundle map, where $1\le p\le\dim V$. If $s_0,\ldots,s_r$ are sections of the same positive power $L^{\otimes m}$, with $s_0\ne0$, then $$\label{eq:wedge-ratio}
 d(s_a/s_0)\wedge i(L)=0$$ at the generic point. In particular, $\kappa(L)\le p$. If $\kappa(L)=p$, there are such sections $s_0,\ldots,s_p$ for which the image line of $i$ is generically spanned by $$\label{eq:wedge-description}
 d(s_1/s_0)\wedge\cdots\wedge d(s_p/s_0)\ne0.$$
